{
 "id": 24,
 "number": 22,
 "title": "Generate Parentheses",
 "slug": "generate-parentheses",
 "category": "stack",
 "difficulty": "Medium",
 "url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/generate-parentheses/",
 "pattern": "Backtracking with open / close counts",
 "statement": "Given `n` pairs of parentheses, generate **every** well-formed combination. For n = 3 there are five, such as `((()))` and `()(())`.",
 "example": {
  "input": "n = 3",
  "output": "[\"((()))\",\"(()())\",\"(())()\",\"()(())\",\"()()()\"]",
  "why": "These are the only 5 ways to arrange three ( and three ) so that every ) closes an earlier (."
 },
 "more": [
  {
   "input": "n = 1",
   "output": "[\"()\"]"
  },
  {
   "input": "n = 2",
   "output": "[\"(())\",\"()()\"]"
  }
 ],
 "idea": [
  "Build the string one character at a time, and only ever make moves that keep it valid — then every finished string is automatically well-formed.",
  "Rule 1: a `(` may be added while fewer than `n` have been used.",
  "Rule 2: a `)` may be added only while there are more `(` than `)` so far, so it has something to close. Try both moves wherever they are allowed (backtracking)."
 ],
 "code": "class Solution:\n    def generateParenthesis(self, n: int) -> List[str]:\n        def backtrack(s, open_count, close_count):\n            if len(s) == 2 * n:\n                result.append(s)\n                return\n\n            if open_count < n:\n                backtrack(s + \"(\", open_count + 1, close_count)\n            if close_count < open_count:\n                backtrack(s + \")\", open_count, close_count + 1)\n\n        result = []\n        backtrack(\"\", 0, 0)\n        return result",
 "complexity": {
  "time": "O(4ⁿ / √n)",
  "timeWhy": "There are about 4ⁿ / (n · √n) valid strings (the Catalan numbers), and each one takes O(n) to build.",
  "space": "O(n)",
  "spaceWhy": "The recursion is 2n deep (not counting the output list)."
 },
